---
// The about page, which says plainly that the artwork is machine generated.
//
// That sentence is the single most important one on the site. The shop is
// selling computer-generated pictures, in volume, on a new domain - and if
// a reviewer works that out from the catalogue rather than from the page,
// the shop looks like it was hiding it. Saying it first, clearly, turns the
// biggest liability into an ordinary product description. It is also simply
// true, and "offers that represent you or your products in a way that isn't
// accurate" is the rule being avoided.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { B } from '../lib/shop';
---

<Base
  title={`About ${B.brand}`}
  description={`${B.brand} makes framed art prints to order in the United Kingdom. The artwork is digitally created, the printing and framing are done here, and nothing is sold as a painting or an original.`}
>
  <div class="wrap page narrow">
    <h1>About {B.brand}</h1>

    <p class="prose" style="font-size:1.05rem">
      We make framed art prints in the United Kingdom, one order at a time.
      No warehouse, no stock sitting in boxes — your print is made after you
      buy it and posted in a few days.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the artwork comes from</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Our designs are <strong>digitally created</strong>. They are generated
      with image software rather than painted by hand, then reviewed,
      colour-corrected and cropped by us before anything reaches the shop.
      We say so on every product page as well as here, because it is the
      sort of thing a customer is entitled to know before they spend money.
    </p>
    <p class="prose">
      So, to be unambiguous: nothing we sell is a painting, an original, a
      limited edition or a signed work, and we never describe it as one. It
      is a good print of a picture, framed properly, at a price that makes
      sense for what it is.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do add</h2>
    <ul class="prose">
      <li><strong>Editing.</strong> Designs are checked individually. Ones
        with the wrong details, muddy tone or spoiled composition are
        thrown out rather than listed.</li>
      <li><strong>Subjects worth having.</strong> Named British places,
        species by their proper names, specific objects. Not generic
        wallpaper.</li>
      <li><strong>The printing and framing.</strong> Heavyweight matte art
        paper, wood moulding, glazing, hanging fixture fitted, packed in
        protective board.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we will not sell</h2>
    <ul class="prose">
      <li>Anything using someone else's characters, logos, film or music
        artwork, or other protected property.</li>
      <li>Anything presented as hand-made, original or artist-signed.</li>
      <li>Fake reviews, invented star ratings or pretend scarcity. We have
        been trading a short time and we are not going to dress that up.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who you are buying from</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      {B.legal_name}, a company registered in England and Wales, company
      number {B.company_number}, VAT number {B.vat_number}. Our registered
      office and full contact details are on the
      {' '}<a href="/contact">contact page</a>, and a real person answers
      {' '}<a href={`mailto:${B.email}`}>{B.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
